A place's virtual time takes what its account lacks for counts, whatever the units, rather than TIME_UNITS / units counts for each.
A thread with many units would be due as late as one with a single unit,
and a request would lie further ahead of its virtual time than its span.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a request is due further ahead than its span
Report: a request waits due later than a lender's would be
Witness: fuzz lend-lender-woken

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -341,7 +341,7 @@ static struct place *unit_first(uint32_t unit)
  */
 static uint32_t vtime(const struct place *p)
 {
-    uint32_t full = p->stamp * timer_tick_counts() + (account_cap(p) - p->balance) / place_units(p);
+    uint32_t full = p->stamp * timer_tick_counts() + (account_cap(p) - p->balance);
     uint32_t now = count_of(p) * timer_tick_counts();
     return tick_before(now, full) ? full : now;
 }
